      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: incomplete—event evidence requires authorized access\n\nI verified the following for Modine’s Racine operation:\n\n| Item | Verified value |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Product | Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Recorded period status | **PENDING_CLOSE** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n\nThe source timestamp does not specify a timezone.\n\n**I cannot verify whether a cost event was created after Pending Close from the records I’m authorized to use.** Those records contain no cost-event rows, while the supporting event records require records-custodian access. Consequently, the source transaction, event amount, exact event-created time, minutes late, recorded accounting status, and status-consistency conclusion remain unverified. I requested an authorized event extract and submitted the partial report as **needs evidence**.\n\n### Applicable Oracle policy\n\nOracle’s *Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B* documentation, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting” (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that:\n\n- New transactions created after Pending Close that fall in the current or an earlier period are **not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting** until the period is closed or reopened.\n- Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, including those in error.\n- Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions that continue processing.\n\nThus, processing an ordinary newly created transaction while the applicable period remains Pending Close would be inconsistent with that treatment—but I cannot establish the event-specific finding without authorized evidence.\n\n**No database records were changed.**",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
